<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-RESULTS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-RESULTS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>BARCELONA 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the European</p>
<p>basketball championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>Third and fourth place game:</p>
<p>Russia 97 Greece 77 (halftime 43-43)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Russia: Mikhail Mikhailov 35, Vassily Karassev 19, Igor</p>
<p>Koudelin 12, Sergei Panov 11, Evgueny Kissourin 8.</p>
<p>Greece: Efthimis Rentzias 28, Nicolaos Ekonomou 12, George</p>
<p>Sigalas 9, Evangelos Koronios 6, Fragiskos Alvertis 5, Theofanis</p>
<p>Christodoulou 5.</p>
<p>Russia win bronze medal.</p>
<p>Games to decide 5th to eight places:</p>
<p>Lithuania 93 Spain 94 (halftime 44-40)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Lithuania: Arturas Karnisovas 32, Virgilius Praskevicius 18,</p>
<p>Sarunas Jasikevicius 13, Gintaras Einkis 12, Eurelitus Zukauskas</p>
<p>7.</p>
<p>Spain: Alberto Herreros 20, Ferran Martinez 19, Alberto</p>
<p>Angulo 17, Rafael Jofresa 7, Nacho Rodriguez 6.</p>
<p>Poland 89 Turkey 87 (77-77 at end of 40 minutes, overtime</p>
<p>played, halftime 43-34)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Poland: Maciej Zielinski 17, Robert Kosciuk 16, Tomasz</p>
<p>Jankowski 13, Piotr Szybilski 11, Adam Wojcik 7.</p>
<p>Turkey. Ibrahim Kutluay 29, Ufuk Sarica 15, Mirsad Turkcan</p>
<p>12, Huseyin Besok 10, Oyguc Tamer 6.</p>
<p>Final standings 5 to 8:</p>
<p>5th Spain</p>
<p>6th Lithuania</p>
<p>7th Poland</p>
<p>8th Turkey</p>
</text>
